  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is config_002: RNA-only, multiprofile, PCA, avgpool, with 0.591 accuracy and 0.573 F1, clearly better than single-profile RNA, transformer aggregation, and image-only ResNet. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the RNA representation itself can be improved beyond PCA while keeping the currently best profile and aggregation fixed. config_005 tests scvi_n200 under the same multiprofile + avgpool setting, isolating the effect of the RNA encoder. This is a more efficient next step than moving to multimodal fusion, because image-only evidence is weak and adding image/fusion would confound the RNA encoder question."
}

